# From "One-Month Patterning" (Wave II - Threshold, CD2-3). The tape repeats
# the identical build-and-release cycle for seven subjects in turn (physical
# body, mental self, emotional self, greater self, where you desire to be,
# what you desire to do, what you desire to achieve); written here with one
# full statement of the method, then the seven subjects named against it,
# rather than seven near-verbatim repeats of the same instruction.

@segment  patterning
@title    Patterning
@levels   F12
@duration ~4m

say From Focus 12, you'll create new patterns in your total being, one at a time.
pause 5
say For each one: think of the pattern as already complete — an active reality of your total self, doing and being exactly as you desire. Build it. Make it stronger, more and more. Then release it, and let it flow out strongly into every part of your expanded awareness, in every direction. The pattern leaves your center of consciousness and moves out into all of it.
pause 10
say First, your physical body. The pattern you'd like it to be. Build it.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your mental self. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your emotional self. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your greater self. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now where you desire to be. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now what you desire to do. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now what you desire to achieve. Build the pattern.
pause 18
say Release it.
pause 6
say Relax, and know the pattern is complete — the one you've built for your own existence.
pause 8
